Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:52:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vless, hysteria2, tuic: manage users through the SSM API

Upstream, these inbounds take their users only from the configuration.
They now implement the SSM API's user updates, so the API adds, changes
and removes users on a running inbound, without a restart and without
dropping other users' sessions. VLESS takes a UUID, or
uuid:xtls-rprx-vision; TUIC takes uuid:password; Hysteria2 takes the
password. Users are keyed by name rather than by their place in the
list, so connections in flight stay counted for the right user when the
list changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
